{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1491109-more-power-psions-and-novas-under-the-talent-rules","id":1491109,"title":"More Power! Psions and Novas under the Talent rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-23T11:40:16-07:00","id":1491109,"title":"More Power! Psions and Novas under the Talent rules","content":"So, I purchased <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a>'s excellent <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/402831/House-Rules--Quantum\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules: Quantum</a> Nexus supplement which, among other things, provides guidelines as to how to use the rules for Novas to model stalwarts, Superiors, Sub-Aberrants, and psiads; and it made me wonder if something similar could be done with the rules for Talents. I know that mesmerists and stalwarts already do so; and I'd almost certainly use that as my starting point for this project. <br /> <br /> But how would you modify that to provide for the equivalent of Novas and psions? In the former case, would it be enough to remove the cap on Scale and maybe add a handful of Dynamic Gifts to cover Nova powers that can't be modeled with the existing Dynamic Gifts? For psions, would it mainly be a case of restructuring and extending the Psychic Gifts (e.g., splitting the Biological, Cognitive, and Energetic categories to into subcategories corresponding to the Aptitudes, and adding some more potent Gifts to represent powers available to psions but not psiads; and then restricting each psion to one subcategory), or would there need to be some underlying structural changes as well? <br /> <br /> The idea behind this approach is to allow for the inclusion of Novas and psions in games that otherwise use just the Talents rules, without having to purchase and use the rules from TC:\u00c6on or TC:Aberrant to do so. But would the amount of additional material needed to make this work make it a moot point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T11:56:11-07:00","id":1491111,"title":"","content":"I am playing with the idea of making all characters based in Inspiration (I love the Facets), but I didnt plan to go all the way in that direction... but now I am... Damn you! The idea is just too good to be left alone...<br /> <br /> By the way, thanks for buying and THANK YOU for the compliment!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-23-2022, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T12:53:34-07:00","id":1491114,"title":"","content":"On a quick think about the subject:<br /> - Aberrant system is very flexible to be completely turned into a set of gifts without a monstruous effort, but a possible idea is to have a few sets of powers with a &quot;Gift Tree&quot; that may direct those powers to certain concepts, like the set presented in Adventure! with the Cold thematic effects and the Heat thematic effects. It would make FAR simpler to build a Nova, but would make them much more restricted in the options of fluffy.<br /> - Maxing out and Power Stunts become more like Dramatic Editing and less &quot;success for a dot&quot;<br /> - I would not go in the direction of Transcendence, but transformations could be Conditions that when come to play grant Inspiration instead of Moment, allow them to use more powers more often if they are weird.<br /> - Psi powers are far more simple to simulate as they are pretty limited in fluffy, but the way they work as skills that can do a lot is hard to model as . I would maybe make something like each mode of an aptitude be based in a facet and they gain gifts that evolve according to the facet grow instead of many gifts that evolve.<br /> <br /> On a alternative approach that can work for both templates, the character may gain gifts that allow them to gain dots in skills and with those skills do powers by paying Inspiration, like the Psi Modes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T12:56:11-07:00","id":1491115,"title":"","content":"If it leads to a House Rules: Inspiration that's akin to House Rules: Quantum, it will be worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T13:48:16-07:00","id":1491121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1491109-more-power-psions-and-novas-under-the-talent-rules?p=1491114#post1491114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a quick think about the subject:<br /> - Aberrant system is very flexible to be completely turned into a set of gifts without a monstruous effort, but a possible idea is to have a few sets of powers with a &amp;quot;Gift Tree&amp;quot; that may direct those powers to certain concepts, like the set presented in Adventure! with the Cold thematic effects and the Heat thematic effects. It would make FAR simpler to build a Nova, but would make them much more restricted in the options of fluffy.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about something kind of like your Techniques construction system from <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/301201/Fists-of-Flux\" target=\"_blank\">Fists of Flux</a>, but repurposed to represent Dynamic Gifts instead of martial arts maneuvers? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1491109-more-power-psions-and-novas-under-the-talent-rules?p=1491114#post1491114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> - Maxing out and Power Stunts become more like Dramatic Editing and less &amp;quot;success for a dot&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, the rules for stalwarts already have something more or less to this effect. I think? <br /> <br /> More thoughts on the rest of this later, what I have some more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T16:12:55-07:00","id":1491138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1491109-more-power-psions-and-novas-under-the-talent-rules#post1491109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea behind this approach is to allow for the inclusion of Novas and psions in games that otherwise use just the Talents rules, without having to purchase and use the rules from TC:\u00c6on or TC:Aberrant to do so. But would the amount of additional material needed to make this work make it a moot point?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Magog rules from Aether already let you play nova level characters using Gifts.<br /> <br /> There are several Magog Gifts that boost a type of Scale by one of your Facets (ie. Endurance of Steel boosts Durability Scale by your Destructive Facet); two are Destructive, three are Intuitive, and two are Reflective. Stick one dot in each Facet and choose the proper Gifts to gain Scale 2 in any areas of your choice or stick three dots in a single Facet to gain Scale 4 to a more limited range of Gifts.<br /> <br /> The Paragon Gift can be taken up to nine times (once per Attribute), and each purchase boosts a type of Scale. Multiple purchases let you boost your Speed, Durability, and Leadership Scales by 2. This probably stacks with the previous Gifts and may stack with edges like Swift and Strongman. You could get a starting character with Scale 6 Durability or Leadership, or Scale 7 Power or Speed. Investing 10 xp in the same Facet (two sessions worth of xp) gets you to Scale 8 or 9. This is far more power than a beginning nova.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T00:55:40-07:00","id":1491165,"title":"","content":"The idea for novas powers is not as much as power as it is versatility as I see.<br /> <br /> Using Adventure Stalwart gifts and removing the limit of 2 times for Paragon Gift you can create a more linear grow and reach as much power as you want, or use the Magog option and grow fast and cause deviations, fit the idea of aberrant as well as Magogs.<br /> <br /> The problem is you have SO MANY options for powers in the comics (many different energies, many different ways to command it, many different combinations) that the only way to do it without a list with hundreds of powers is something versatile like TC Aberrant did. No redundant powers like 1e system (no problem with that, just so many times you are referring to another power, specially among level 3 powers).<br /> <br /> If you have a comprehensible list of powers, it would have part of Aberrant feeling, but there would always be that guy saying why don\u2019t we have \u201cblank, blank, blank\u201d. I mean, if the idea is keep it within a certain limit it\u2019s ok, but\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T01:07:50-07:00","id":1491166,"title":"","content":"Following what I had previously written about using Inspiration as the only measure of how you interact with your source for Psi and Quantum.<br /> <br /> <b>It was Inspiration All Along</b><br /> Inspiration, as presented in Trinity Continuum Core Rulebook has many interesting impacts over the game that are lost in the way Psi and Quantum works. It\u2019s possible to switch back that, turning Inspiration in the measure of the character control over their powers, no matter what power source it is. There are a few changes in the way it works, as it impacts all aspects previously related to Psi and Quantum, the prerequisites in certain powers and aptitudes, and the way you spend Inspiration to use powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychic Inspiration</b><br /> Inspiration replaces Psi as the measure of control over psi a character have. It replaces the use of Psi whenever it affects difficulties to affect the character, to define the Formatting Tolerance of the character and to define travel time using Teleportation modes.<br /> <br /> <b>Psion Template and Advancement</b><br /> The Psion template remains exactly the same except for, instead of receiving Psi 2, the Psion gains 3 dots to distribute among the 3 facets. During step 6 of character creation, the Psion can exchange the Attribute dot by a Facet dot. Increasing each facet by 1 dot costs 10 experience, but the Psion can only have up to 4 dots in each Facet. Inspiration Effects Psi have many impacts in the powers of a Psion that are all attributed to specific facets, following the tables below.<br /> When the Psion achieves Inspiration 6, the mastery they have over Psi changes their target number 7, allow them to gain the 6th dot in their aptitude modes, 2nd dot in auxiliary modes and 6th dot in all attributes (without the Superior Trait Edge), adds 1 dice to any facet roll and regains two points of Inspiration at the start of each new scene. Achieving Inspiration 7 allows the Psion to gain 7th dot powers of their aptitudes, increases the Size and Combat scale by 1, the Attunement range by 1 range band (or 10 times for Extreme) and 2 dice to any facet roll (not cumulative with psi 6).<br /> <br /> Inspiration ... Primary ... Auxiliary ... TN<br /> 3 .................... 5 ............ 1 .............. 8<br /> 4 .................... 5 ............ 1 .............. 8<br /> 5 .................... 5 ............ 1 .............. 8<br /> 6 .................... 6 ............ 2 .............. 7<br /> 7 .................... 7 ............ 2 .............. 7<br /> <br /> <b>Quantakinesis and Teleportation</b><br /> Quantakinesis and Teleportation have a minimum Inspiration of 4 instead of Psi 3. It\u2019s won\u2019t force increasing their Psi by exchanging an Attribute dot for Psi as before, only requiring a specific distribution of facet dots. Facet Effects Psi have many impacts in the powers of a Psion that are all attributed to specific facets, following the tables below.<br /> Destructive ... Size <br /> 0 ..................... 0<br /> 1 ..................... 1<br /> 2 ..................... 1<br /> 3 ..................... 2<br /> 4 ..................... 2<br /> Intuitive ... Range ... Attunement Range<br /> 0 ............. Close ..... Short<br /> 1 ............. Short ...... Medium<br /> 2 ............. Short ...... Long<br /> 3 ............. Medium .. Extreme (10 kilometer)<br /> 4 ............. Long ....... Extreme (100 kilometer)<br /> Reflective ... Duration<br /> 0 ................. Rounds<br /> 1 ................. Rounds<br /> 2 ................. Minutes<br /> 3 ................. Hours<br /> 4 ................. Days<br /> <br /> <b>Power Dice Pools</b><br /> All powers that dice pools were Psi + Mode become Facet + Mode, and the chosen facet is defined by the approach intended with the power, Destructive for Force approach, Intuitive for Finesse approach and Reflective for Resilience approach. It includes regular uses of power and when power reaching.<br /> <br /> <b>Spending and Recovering Inspiration</b><br /> A Psion may spend Inspiration the same way as a talent, except for not being able to Dramatic Edition (optionally the Storyguide may make it possible). The same way, a Psion also recovers Inspiration as a Talent, except Psions require exposure to psi to recover, instead of flux. Psions can also recover Inspiration equal to their Reflective facet by spending a scene meditating.<br /> Psi powers require spending 1 Inspiration for every psi of its cost, including additional psi to expand effects and reaching higher mode dots. When using powers of lower mode dots, each mode dot above it reduces the cost by 1 point, in addition to other effects, to a minimum of 0 Inspiration. Some powers suffer small changes to better fit the system.<br /> Drain (Quantakinesis, Fundamentals 3): The psion takes one Inspiration or Corruption from her target per success, adding Inspiration to her pool or the pool of any single psion within his Range at a rate of one Inspiration point per 2 Inspiration or Corruption drained.<br /> <br /> <b>Empowering</b><br /> Combining powers and super science that increase Psi instead increase an specific facet, if it usually limited to Psi 5, it may increase the Facet up to 3, if it was limited to Psi 7, it may increase the Facet up to 4. Some powers suffer small changes to better fit the system.<br /> Empowerment (Vitakinesis, Augendis 3): Instead of increasing separated aspects of the patient psi, the Vitakinetic increases one of the facets by 1 per 3 successes up to 4.<br /> <br /> <b>Quantum Powered Inspiration</b><br /> Inspiration replaces Quantum as the measure of control over quantum a character have. It replaces the use of Quantum whenever it affects difficulties to affect the character, to define the maximum number of Q-Tech that can be attuned and to define travel time using Warp and Teleportation.<br /> <br /> <b>Nova Template and Advancement</b><br /> The Nova template remains the same except for, instead of receiving Quantum 1, the Nova gains 1 dot to set to any of the 3 facets. Each Facet works as an independent Nova Trait, costing 12 experience, and can be bought by half the cost if the nova also takes a point of Transcendence at that time.<br /> <br /> <b>Spending and Recovering Inspiration</b><br /> A Nova may spend Inspiration the same way as a talent, except for not being able to Dramatic Edition (optionally the Storyguide may make it possible). The same way, a Nova also recovers Inspiration as a Talent, except novas require exposure to quantum to recover, instead of flux.<br /> A Nova may also use a reflexive action to gain 1 Flux and recover immediately their Destructive Facet Inspiration. The cost of each Quantum Power or Mega-Edge is reduced by half the related Facet (round up), to a minimum of 0.<br /> Some powers suffer small changes to better fit the system.<br /> Absorption: The power works as described, except that, instead of recovering Quantum Points, the character receives 1 point of Inspiration for every 2 successes. Check Overcharge bellow for more information about the excess of Inspiration.<br /> Quantum Leech: The power works as described, except that, instead of taking the target\u2019s Quantum Points, the character takes 1 point of Inspiration for every 2 successes and adds to their own. Check Overcharge bellow for more information about the excess of Inspiration.<br /> Vampiric Tag: If the Nova has the quantum absorbing option, each injury caused to the target the nova regains 1 Inspiration.<br /> <br /> <b>Overcharge</b><br /> Some Novas can absorb energies to recharge their Inspiration. The rules for Overcharge don\u2019t change, except for trading Quantum Points for Inspiration.<br /> A nova with more than their normal amount of Inspiration acquires either the Aberrant Eyes or Anima Aura transformation, as their nova nature literally shines out.<br /> When they have 3 or more above their normal amount of Inspiration, they acquire both previous transformations as well as the Energy Bleed transformation, giving off random sparks or flashes of energy.<br /> At 5 or more above their normal, the nova acquires the Energy Emissions transformation, barely able to contain the sheer amount of power. For each minute the nova remains at this level of Inspiration, they also suffer either an Injury Condition or acquire a point of Flux, as the nova\u2019s player chooses, until their Inspiration total drops below 5 above normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Burn Out</b><br /> For every Inspiration a nova expends after reaching zero Inspiration, the nova takes an Injury Condition. This is considered lethal damage, and novas can be Taken Out by this damage (commonly known as \u201cburning out\u201d). The nova suffers the Injury Condition after taking the action where they spend the Inspiration.<br /> <br /> <b>Power Dice Pools</b><br /> All powers that dice pools wereL Quantum + Power become Facet + Power, and the chosen facet is defined by the approach intended with the power, Destructive for Force approach, Intuitive for Finesse approach and Reflective for Resilience approach. It includes regular uses of power and when power stunting.<br /> When Novas reaches Inspiration 6, the mastery they have over Quantum grants them 1 enhancement in all Facet + Power Rolls, including power stunts.<br /> At Inspiration 7 it increases to 2 enhancements, at Inspiration 8 to 3 enhancements and at 9 to 4 enhancements.<br /> <br /> <b>Quantum Minimum and Prerequisites</b><br /> Quantum cease to be the reference of the character power, giving its place to individual Facets, affecting all Mega-Attributes and Quantum Powers. Force Mega-Attributes have Facet Minimum (like Quantum Minimum) equal to Destructive Dots, Finesse Mega-Attributes have Facet Minimum (like Quantum Minimum) equal to Intuitive Dots and Resilience Mega-Attributes have Facet Minimum (like Quantum Minimum) equal to Reflective Dots. Quantum powers, instead of Quantum Minimum, have a Facet Minimum, with the related facet defined according to the following list.<br /> For example, to have dots in Flight, the Nova must have at least the same number of dots in Intuitive Facet (previously Quantum Minimum was Dots), and to have dots in Quantum Imprint, the character must have at least 4 dots in Destructive facet (previously Quantum Minimum was 4).<br /> Power ............................... Facet Minimum<br /> Absorption ........................ Reflective 2<br /> Boost ................................ Destructive Dots<br /> Cloak ................................ Intuitive 2<br /> Density ............................. Reflective Dots<br /> Elemental Mastery ........... Intuitive 2<br /> Environmental Anima ....... Destructive Dots<br /> Flight ................................ Intuitive Dots<br /> Growth ............................. Reflective Dots<br /> Healing ............................ Destructive 2<br /> Illusion ............................. Intuitive 2<br /> Molecular Chameleon ..... Reflective 4<br /> Molecular Manipulation ... Intuitive 3<br /> Morph .............................. Destructive Dots -3<br /> Phasing ........................... Intuitive 2<br /> Plasticity .......................... Reflective 2<br /> Quantum Agent ............... Destructive Dots<br /> Quantum Anima .............. Intuitive Dots<br /> Quantum Attack .............. Destructive Dots<br /> Quantum Aura ................ Destructive Dots<br /> Quantum Construct ........ Intuitive Dots +1<br /> Quantum Deflection ........ Reflective Dots<br /> Quantum Disruption ........ Reflective 3<br /> Quantum Field ................ Reflective Dots<br /> Quantum Imprint ............. Destructive 4<br /> Quantum Leech .............. Destructive 2<br /> Remote Perception ......... Intuitive 3<br /> Shrinking ........................ Reflective Dots -1<br /> Shroud ........................... Reflective 2<br /> Teleport .......................... Intuitive Dots +1<br /> Transformation ............... Destructive 4<br /> Transmutation ................ Destructive 4<br /> Warp .............................. Intuitive Dots +2<br /> Technique Mega-Edge prerequisites become Intuitive facet equal to Edge Dots, and Toughness Mega-Edge prerequisites become Reflective facet equal to Edge Dots. Inspiration is also the maximum cost of any tag the character may have in their powers.<br /> When Novas reaches Inspiration 6, they reduce by 1 the Facet Minimum of all their Quantum Powers and Mega-Attributes dots by 1, as well as the prerequisites in Facets. For example, if a Nova has Destructive 3 and Intuitive 5 (Inspiration 6), the character may have Quantum Attack 4, Mega Dexterity 6 and Toughness 1.<br /> At Inspiration 7 the Facet Minimum and Prerequisites are reduced by 2, at Inspiration 8 by 3 and at 9 by 4.<br /> <br /> <b>Transcendence</b><br /> Without Quantum trait, a Nova increase Transcendence by 1 when reach 4 and 5 in each of the Facets.<br /> <br /> <b>Advancement and Maxing Out</b><br /> Novas can\u2019t max out Inspiration itself, instead they max out each Facet independently. A Nova just need to max out a Facet once before increasing it, as for every other nova Trait. The Nova spend 1 Inspiration and gains 1 Flux, rolls Inspiration and each success can grant a single nova trait. Spending 1 Inspiration<br /> <br /> <b>Super Science</b><br /> When building Q-tech, a nova inventor must meet the Facet minimums for any power she builds into a device, but she need not possess the power herself. When attuning Q-tech, a nova must meet the Facet minimums for any power built into the device. Attuning to a Q-Tech costs 1 Inspiration, but it is not imbued to the item nor can\u2019t be recovered. When the Attunement is broken the Nova don\u2019t receive back any Inspiration. Activating an attuned Q-Tech also don\u2019t requires committing Inspiration, instead it requires the character pay 1 Inspiration if the Q-Tech have any Intrinsic power (the spent Inspiration can be recovered as usual) when first activating it, plus the cost of any other power when using them. It is possible for novas who are not attuned to a Q-tech device to gain some limited use from it. The player rolls the nova\u2019s highest Facet, and on a success can use the device for one Scene before it shuts down","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-24-2022, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T09:05:31-07:00","id":1491198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1491109-more-power-psions-and-novas-under-the-talent-rules?p=1491165#post1491165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea for novas powers is not as much as power as it is versatility as I see.<br /> <br /> Using Adventure Stalwart gifts and removing the limit of 2 times for Paragon Gift you can create a more linear grow and reach as much power as you want, or use the Magog option and grow fast and cause deviations, fit the idea of aberrant as well as Magogs.<br /> <br /> The problem is you have SO MANY options for powers in the comics (many different energies, many different ways to command it, many different combinations) that the only way to do it without a list with hundreds of powers is something versatile like TC Aberrant did. No redundant powers like 1e system (no problem with that, just so many times you are referring to another power, specially among level 3 powers).<br /> <br /> If you have a comprehensible list of powers, it would have part of Aberrant feeling, but there would always be that guy saying why don\u2019t we have \u201cblank, blank, blank\u201d. I mean, if the idea is keep it within a certain limit it\u2019s ok, but\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>That versatility was part of the reason why I was suggesting that you might want to rework your Techniques from fists of flux as a sort of guideline for creating new dynamic gifts. Although the fact that your techniques have dot ratings and dynamic gifts do not could be problematic. At the very least, though, I think the solution should be more robust guidelines for creating your own dynamic gifts. Something that goes beyond the guidelines provided in adventure, to give a better idea of what sorts of options are possible, and what reasonable implementations of them would look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T09:32:16-07:00","id":1491200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1491109-more-power-psions-and-novas-under-the-talent-rules?p=1491198#post1491198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That versatility was part of the reason why I was suggesting that you might want to rework your Techniques from fists of flux as a sort of guideline for creating new dynamic gifts. Although the fact that your techniques have dot ratings and dynamic gifts do not could be problematic. At the very least, though, I think the solution should be more robust guidelines for creating your own dynamic gifts. Something that goes beyond the guidelines provided in adventure, to give a better idea of what sorts of options are possible, and what reasonable implementations of them would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you point, the different costs could be a problem with moving Techniques to Powers. I like the way I did wit hTechniques, but it creates a certain complexity in creating different powers, specially if you dont have a few to explain how the resulting may look (that is what I see as the biggest flaw of my book, restropectively).<br /> <br /> I may suggest something more like a Gift Tree that take a few starting gifts and expand them to higher levels of power or flexibility.<br /> Just to give an idea of what I mean:<br /> Gift A allow you to condict electricit with your body.<br /> Gift B for storing electricity in your body (prerequisite in A).<br /> Gift C allows absorbing and shooting it at distance (prerequisite in A).<br /> Gift D creates electricity yourself (prerequisite in B).<br /> Gift E allow you to control electricity out of your body directly (prerequisite in C).<br /> Gift F allow you to control magnetism (prerequisite in D and E)<br /> Gift G allow to area attack with electricity (prerequisite in C)<br /> Gift H allow to increase the amount of turn into Electricity (prerequisite in B and E)<br /> <br /> It creates something like:<br /> A -- B -- D<br /> | H &lt; ..... |<br /> C -- E -- F<br /> |<br /> G","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-24-2022, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T09:55:34-07:00","id":1491205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1491109-more-power-psions-and-novas-under-the-talent-rules?p=1491166#post1491166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following what I had previously written about using Inspiration as the only measure of how you interact with your source for Psi and Quantum.<br /> <br /> <b>It was Inspiration All Along</b><br /> Inspiration, as presented in Trinity Continuum Core Rulebook has many interesting impacts over the game that are lost in the way Psi and Quantum works. It\u2019s possible to switch back that, turning Inspiration in the measure of the character control over their powers, no matter what power source it is. There are a few changes in the way it works, as it impacts all aspects previously related to Psi and Quantum, the prerequisites in certain powers and aptitudes, and the way you spend Inspiration to use powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychic Inspiration</b><br /> Inspiration replaces Psi as the measure of control over psi a character have. It replaces the use of Psi whenever it affects difficulties to affect the character, to define the Formatting Tolerance of the character and to define travel time using Teleportation modes.<br /> <br /> <b>Psion Template and Advancement</b><br /> The Psion template remains exactly the same except for, instead of receiving Psi 2, the Psion gains 3 dots to distribute among the 3 facets. During step 6 of character creation, the Psion can exchange the Attribute dot by a Facet dot. Increasing each facet by 1 dot costs 10 experience, but the Psion can only have up to 4 dots in each Facet. Inspiration Effects Psi have many impacts in the powers of a Psion that are all attributed to specific facets, following the tables below.<br /> When the Psion achieves Inspiration 6, the mastery they have over Psi changes their target number 7, allow them to gain the 6th dot in their aptitude modes, 2nd dot in auxiliary modes and 6th dot in all attributes (without the Superior Trait Edge), adds 1 dice to any facet roll and regains two points of Inspiration at the start of each new scene. Achieving Inspiration 7 allows the Psion to gain 7th dot powers of their aptitudes, increases the Size and Combat scale by 1, the Attunement range by 1 range band (or 10 times for Extreme) and 2 dice to any facet roll (not cumulative with psi 6).<br /> <br /> Inspiration ... Primary ... Auxiliary ... TN<br /> 3 .................... 5 ............ 1 .............. 8<br /> 4 .................... 5 ............ 1 .............. 8<br /> 5 .................... 5 ............ 1 .............. 8<br /> 6 .................... 6 ............ 2 .............. 7<br /> 7 .................... 7 ............ 2 .............. 7<br /> <br /> <b>Quantakinesis and Teleportation</b><br /> Quantakinesis and Teleportation have a minimum Inspiration of 4 instead of Psi 3. It\u2019s won\u2019t force increasing their Psi by exchanging an Attribute dot for Psi as before, only requiring a specific distribution of facet dots. Facet Effects Psi have many impacts in the powers of a Psion that are all attributed to specific facets, following the tables below.<br /> Destructive ... Size <br /> 0 ..................... 0<br /> 1 ..................... 1<br /> 2 ..................... 1<br /> 3 ..................... 2<br /> 4 ..................... 2<br /> Intuitive ... Range ... Attunement Range<br /> 0 ............. Close ..... Short<br /> 1 ............. Short ...... Medium<br /> 2 ............. Short ...... Long<br /> 3 ............. Medium .. Extreme (10 kilometer)<br /> 4 ............. Long ....... Extreme (100 kilometer)<br /> Reflective ... Duration<br /> 0 ................. Rounds<br /> 1 ................. Rounds<br /> 2 ................. Minutes<br /> 3 ................. Hours<br /> 4 ................. Days<br /> <br /> <b>Power Dice Pools</b><br /> All powers that dice pools were Psi + Mode become Facet + Mode, and the chosen facet is defined by the approach intended with the power, Destructive for Force approach, Intuitive for Finesse approach and Reflective for Resilience approach. It includes regular uses of power and when power reaching.<br /> <br /> <b>Spending and Recovering Inspiration</b><br /> A Psion may spend Inspiration the same way as a talent, except for not being able to Dramatic Edition (optionally the Storyguide may make it possible). The same way, a Psion also recovers Inspiration as a Talent, except Psions require exposure to psi to recover, instead of flux. Psions can also recover Inspiration equal to their Reflective facet by spending a scene meditating.<br /> Psi powers require spending 1 Inspiration for every psi of its cost, including additional psi to expand effects and reaching higher mode dots. When using powers of lower mode dots, each mode dot above it reduces the cost by 1 point, in addition to other effects, to a minimum of 0 Inspiration. Some powers suffer small changes to better fit the system.<br /> Drain (Quantakinesis, Fundamentals 3): The psion takes one Inspiration or Corruption from her target per success, adding Inspiration to her pool or the pool of any single psion within his Range at a rate of one Inspiration point per 2 Inspiration or Corruption drained.<br /> <br /> <b>Empowering</b><br /> Combining powers and super science that increase Psi instead increase an specific facet, if it usually limited to Psi 5, it may increase the Facet up to 3, if it was limited to Psi 7, it may increase the Facet up to 4. Some powers suffer small changes to better fit the system.<br /> Empowerment (Vitakinesis, Augendis 3): Instead of increasing separated aspects of the patient psi, the Vitakinetic increases one of the facets by 1 per 3 successes up to 4.<br /> <br /> <b>Quantum Powered Inspiration</b><br /> Inspiration replaces Quantum as the measure of control over quantum a character have. It replaces the use of Quantum whenever it affects difficulties to affect the character, to define the maximum number of Q-Tech that can be attuned and to define travel time using Warp and Teleportation.<br /> <br /> <b>Nova Template and Advancement</b><br /> The Nova template remains the same except for, instead of receiving Quantum 1, the Nova gains 1 dot to set to any of the 3 facets. Each Facet works as an independent Nova Trait, costing 12 experience, and can be bought by half the cost if the nova also takes a point of Transcendence at that time.<br /> <br /> <b>Spending and Recovering Inspiration</b><br /> A Nova may spend Inspiration the same way as a talent, except for not being able to Dramatic Edition (optionally the Storyguide may make it possible). The same way, a Nova also recovers Inspiration as a Talent, except novas require exposure to quantum to recover, instead of flux.<br /> A Nova may also use a reflexive action to gain 1 Flux and recover immediately their Destructive Facet Inspiration. The cost of each Quantum Power or Mega-Edge is reduced by half the related Facet (round up), to a minimum of 0.<br /> Some powers suffer small changes to better fit the system.<br /> Absorption: The power works as described, except that, instead of recovering Quantum Points, the character receives 1 point of Inspiration for every 2 successes. Check Overcharge bellow for more information about the excess of Inspiration.<br /> Quantum Leech: The power works as described, except that, instead of taking the target\u2019s Quantum Points, the character takes 1 point of Inspiration for every 2 successes and adds to their own. Check Overcharge bellow for more information about the excess of Inspiration.<br /> Vampiric Tag: If the Nova has the quantum absorbing option, each injury caused to the target the nova regains 1 Inspiration.<br /> <br /> <b>Overcharge</b><br /> Some Novas can absorb energies to recharge their Inspiration. The rules for Overcharge don\u2019t change, except for trading Quantum Points for Inspiration.<br /> A nova with more than their normal amount of Inspiration acquires either the Aberrant Eyes or Anima Aura transformation, as their nova nature literally shines out.<br /> When they have 3 or more above their normal amount of Inspiration, they acquire both previous transformations as well as the Energy Bleed transformation, giving off random sparks or flashes of energy.<br /> At 5 or more above their normal, the nova acquires the Energy Emissions transformation, barely able to contain the sheer amount of power. For each minute the nova remains at this level of Inspiration, they also suffer either an Injury Condition or acquire a point of Flux, as the nova\u2019s player chooses, until their Inspiration total drops below 5 above normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Burn Out</b><br /> For every Inspiration a nova expends after reaching zero Inspiration, the nova takes an Injury Condition. This is considered lethal damage, and novas can be Taken Out by this damage (commonly known as \u201cburning out\u201d). The nova suffers the Injury Condition after taking the action where they spend the Inspiration.<br /> <br /> <b>Power Dice Pools</b><br /> All powers that dice pools wereL Quantum + Power become Facet + Power, and the chosen facet is defined by the approach intended with the power, Destructive for Force approach, Intuitive for Finesse approach and Reflective for Resilience approach. It includes regular uses of power and when power stunting.<br /> When Novas reaches Inspiration 6, the mastery they have over Quantum grants them 1 enhancement in all Facet + Power Rolls, including power stunts.<br /> At Inspiration 7 it increases to 2 enhancements, at Inspiration 8 to 3 enhancements and at 9 to 4 enhancements.<br /> <br /> <b>Quantum Minimum and Prerequisites</b><br /> Quantum cease to be the reference of the character power, giving its place to individual Facets, affecting all Mega-Attributes and Quantum Powers. Force Mega-Attributes have Facet Minimum (like Quantum Minimum) equal to Destructive Dots, Finesse Mega-Attributes have Facet Minimum (like Quantum Minimum) equal to Intuitive Dots and Resilience Mega-Attributes have Facet Minimum (like Quantum Minimum) equal to Reflective Dots. Quantum powers, instead of Quantum Minimum, have a Facet Minimum, with the related facet defined according to the following list.<br /> For example, to have dots in Flight, the Nova must have at least the same number of dots in Intuitive Facet (previously Quantum Minimum was Dots), and to have dots in Quantum Imprint, the character must have at least 4 dots in Destructive facet (previously Quantum Minimum was 4).<br /> Power ............................... Facet Minimum<br /> Absorption ........................ Reflective 2<br /> Boost ................................ Destructive Dots<br /> Cloak ................................ Intuitive 2<br /> Density ............................. Reflective Dots<br /> Elemental Mastery ........... Intuitive 2<br /> Environmental Anima ....... Destructive Dots<br /> Flight ................................ Intuitive Dots<br /> Growth ............................. Reflective Dots<br /> Healing ............................ Destructive 2<br /> Illusion ............................. Intuitive 2<br /> Molecular Chameleon ..... Reflective 4<br /> Molecular Manipulation ... Intuitive 3<br /> Morph .............................. Destructive Dots -3<br /> Phasing ........................... Intuitive 2<br /> Plasticity .......................... Reflective 2<br /> Quantum Agent ............... Destructive Dots<br /> Quantum Anima .............. Intuitive Dots<br /> Quantum Attack .............. Destructive Dots<br /> Quantum Aura ................ Destructive Dots<br /> Quantum Construct ........ Intuitive Dots +1<br /> Quantum Deflection ........ Reflective Dots<br /> Quantum Disruption ........ Reflective 3<br /> Quantum Field ................ Reflective Dots<br /> Quantum Imprint ............. Destructive 4<br /> Quantum Leech .............. Destructive 2<br /> Remote Perception ......... Intuitive 3<br /> Shrinking ........................ Reflective Dots -1<br /> Shroud ........................... Reflective 2<br /> Teleport .......................... Intuitive Dots +1<br /> Transformation ............... Destructive 4<br /> Transmutation ................ Destructive 4<br /> Warp .............................. Intuitive Dots +2<br /> Technique Mega-Edge prerequisites become Intuitive facet equal to Edge Dots, and Toughness Mega-Edge prerequisites become Reflective facet equal to Edge Dots. Inspiration is also the maximum cost of any tag the character may have in their powers.<br /> When Novas reaches Inspiration 6, they reduce by 1 the Facet Minimum of all their Quantum Powers and Mega-Attributes dots by 1, as well as the prerequisites in Facets. For example, if a Nova has Destructive 3 and Intuitive 5 (Inspiration 6), the character may have Quantum Attack 4, Mega Dexterity 6 and Toughness 1.<br /> At Inspiration 7 the Facet Minimum and Prerequisites are reduced by 2, at Inspiration 8 by 3 and at 9 by 4.<br /> <br /> <b>Transcendence</b><br /> Without Quantum trait, a Nova increase Transcendence by 1 when reach 4 and 5 in each of the Facets.<br /> <br /> <b>Advancement and Maxing Out</b><br /> Novas can\u2019t max out Inspiration itself, instead they max out each Facet independently. A Nova just need to max out a Facet once before increasing it, as for every other nova Trait. The Nova spend 1 Inspiration and gains 1 Flux, rolls Inspiration and each success can grant a single nova trait. Spending 1 Inspiration<br /> <br /> <b>Super Science</b><br /> When building Q-tech, a nova inventor must meet the Facet minimums for any power she builds into a device, but she need not possess the power herself. When attuning Q-tech, a nova must meet the Facet minimums for any power built into the device. Attuning to a Q-Tech costs 1 Inspiration, but it is not imbued to the item nor can\u2019t be recovered. When the Attunement is broken the Nova don\u2019t receive back any Inspiration. Activating an attuned Q-Tech also don\u2019t requires committing Inspiration, instead it requires the character pay 1 Inspiration if the Q-Tech have any Intrinsic power (the spent Inspiration can be recovered as usual) when first activating it, plus the cost of any other power when using them. It is possible for novas who are not attuned to a Q-tech device to gain some limited use from it. The player rolls the nova\u2019s highest Facet, and on a success can use the device for one Scene before it shuts down</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea I was thinking of was that you should be able to do this using just TC: Adventure! and a Nexus product; writing it up in a way that the user needs to pull out TC:\u00c6on or TC:Aberrant largely defeats the purpose. If you can build on top of the rules for Mesmerists and Stalwarts so that they end up as a subset of the Inspiration-based Psion and Nova rules (Novas moreso than psions), so much the better. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't mind references to \u00c6on or Aberrant while it's being hashed out; just so long as the final product doesn't need them. <br /> <br /> Adventure gives stalwarts a version of dramatic editing that implements the notion of overcharge. Keep that. But also use that as inspiration (no pun intended) for what to do with Psion dramatic editing. That is, find some mechanic that exists for psions universally; something that would not be appropriate to treat as a psychic Gift; and say that <i>that's</i> what psionic Dramatic Editing does. I nominate Attunement, or something like it: the ability to detect psionic signatures, and to link up to bio ware and to other psions in order to enhance each other's effects. <br /> <br /> More thoughts later; I'm at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:12:41-07:00","id":1491208,"title":"","content":"I got your original idea, I just had to show what I had.<br /> <br /> I like your idea a lot and woul blindly buy it as a CC book, but I think the effort to create it as something self containing is huge if you want to cover all that the psions and novas can do is huge!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:31:20-07:00","id":1491214,"title":"","content":"Agreed, which was part of my initial concern. That said, both for that reason and to not trample on aberrant too much, I would approach it not so much as a full-on design system for dynamic gifts, but rather with the mindset that the player is going to come up with a power concept on her own, and it's our job to provide guidance for her to turn that into mechanics. That's why I was referring to your techniques system: you didn't provide much in the way of technique writeups; you merely provided the tools needed for players to devise their own techniques. Something like that, in principle if not in particular.<br /> <br /> At the very least, I think we should supply a means of adding tags to Dynamic gifts as part of repurposing them for different uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:57:04-07:00","id":1491219,"title":"","content":"I will post here later (when I have my ipad at hand) a few more effects and tags i have written and are not in any of the books (I was planning to create a new one with it, but they are just too few). Feel free to copy the entire chapter in your text and improve it as you wish. I really love the fact people are using my material!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T11:15:57-07:00","id":1491222,"title":"","content":"I would point out that that list of effects is essentially yours; so I don't think anyone would have grounds to complain if you were to reuse it in a different context. If you enrich it with a couple of other effects, even better.<br /> <br /> In that regard, I wonder how the existing stalwart gifts would look if reconstructed using something like the Techniques system. Set aside for the moment the prerequisites or the dot ratings; just, which effect and which tags for each?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T10:56:16-07:00","id":1491430,"title":"","content":"The idea of expanding things so that the Inspiration system covers the higher tiers of Psi and Quantum works for me and sounds super fun. Gifts are a very interesting system and I think there is much potential in expanding it to higher tiers. Honestly, Aether helps with that with the Gog and Magog stuff and so does Adventure! and its Stalwart and Mesmerist Gifts. <br /> <br /> So yeah, this is fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T12:18:55-07:00","id":1491434,"title":"","content":"I am pretty confident the idea of trees of gifts can be a great option to cover both Nova and Psion powers.<br /> <br /> Psion powers could be expanding on the Adventure Psychic Gifts, but I really think for Psions we should go on a tree for each Mode, with some of the Adventure being part of some different trees.<br /> <br /> For Novas gifts we can pick the Dynamic Gifts from Adventure and expand them for the more powerful ones, and add some Magog powers that allow you to gain scale on one or more powers. It can be extremely useful to make a sequence for each scale instead of Mega Attributes like gifts.<br /> <br /> I am willing to spend some of my free time here to organize the gifts from Adventure by themes and modes. If anyone have done it before it would make it FAR easier to me...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T00:12:48-07:00","id":1493891,"title":"","content":"<b>Inspired Psions</b><br /> Psions are artificial Mesmerists, created to fight against the powerful Aberrants, their Gifts is limited to certain focus, yet they are more powerful, exchanging versatility for potency.<br /> Psions have access to psychic gifts of a single Aptitude, defined by the chamber turned them into Psions, Biokinesis, Clairsentience, Electrokinesis, Psychokinesis, Quantakinesis, Telepathy, Teleportation and Vitakinesis. Each Aptitude has a list of possible gifts divided in 3 \u201ctiers\u201d, Auxiliary, Standard and Advanced, all Psions consider their Aptitude Gifts as Path Gifts, and can learn and reach Gifts of all 3 tiers, as long all prerequisites are met. They can also learn Auxiliary tier gifts of any other aptitude, not treated as Path Gifts.<br /> Psions, as well as Psiads, can combine their powers by touching each other and all assisting the primary Psion spending Inspiration and rolling Inspiration, the successes are transferred to the primary Psion roll. It happens Psions are far superior at doing so, granting advantages related to their aptitudes when combining their powers:<br /> Biokinesis: Double the number of successes the primary psion has available to spend, after accounting for Difficulty or Complications.<br /> Clairsentience: Gifts can be used at Inspiration range bands from the clairsentient. In addition, gifts that can reach beyond that, have a maximum range of Inspiration x 10 light years.<br /> Electrokinesis: Multiply the duration of the gifts\u2019s effect by the electrokinetic\u2019s Inspiration trait. If the effect normally lasts an instant \u2014 such as an attack \u2014 the effect can be used again the next round without additional cost.<br /> Psychokinesis: Add the psychokinetic\u2019s Inspiration trait as Enhancement to powers used on objects and devices.<br /> Quantakinesis: Double the primary psion\u2019s facets when calculating dice pools and effects.<br /> Telepathy: Allow the primary psion to affect a number of targets equal to the telepath\u2019s Inspiration with each use of a gift that can normally only affect a single target other than the psion.<br /> Teleportation: Increase the power\u2019s area of effect by one range band. Gifts without an area of effect gain one equal to short.<br /> Vitakinesis: Add the vitakinetic\u2019s Inspiration trait as Enhancement to powers on living creatures.<br /> When a Psion achieve Inspiration 6, her psychic powers expand beyond the levels of regular Psions, and she become capable of learning Psychic Excellences, much similar to the Excellences of Talents, but focused in their Aptitudes instead of Skills. Once learned, Psychic Excellence reduce the target number of any dice pool to 7 (from 8). When the Psion reach 5 dots in a facet, the effects of Excellence improve, granting Aptitude, Intention and Luck effects to it. The effects stack, and a Inspiration 10 Psion gains the 3 effects at same time in all uses of their gifts.<br /> Aptitude: at Reflective Facet 5 the Psion can use any Gift of the Aptitude spending 1 less Inspiration.<br /> Intention: at Destructive Facet 5 the Psion add 1 Scale to all the Aptitude Gifts effects.<br /> Luck: at Intuitive Facet 5 the Psion gains 9-again to all the rolls using the skill.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspired Nova</b><br /> Novas are much similar to Stalwarts, but they are more powerful, far more powerful.<br /> All Novas have a unconscious control over reality, making them more capable than expected, reducing the target number of all dice pool to 7 (from 8).<br /> Novas have access to dynamic gifts, similarly to Stalwarts, but they can reach higher limits of power, not available to regular Stalwarts. Additionally, most Novas eruptions take them to levels of power far above the usual for Stalwarts, granting a higher number of gifts and possibly facet dots, but that values should be defined by the Storyguide, as it may unbalance the game if other templates are available.<br /> Nova powers can be far more powerful than Stalwart ones, as they learn Dynamic Excellences, much similar to the Excellences of Talents, but focused in Dynamic Gifts with specific Attribute keywords or the Power key word instead of Skills. Once learned, Dynamic Excellence increases to the effect of all gifts with the proper keyword, granting half of the related Facet as scale, always rounding up. Force attributes are related to Destructive Facet, Finesse attributes to Intuitive Facet and Resilience attributes to Reflective facet, while Power gifts always use the lowest of the 3 facets.<br /> When a Nova achieve Inspiration 6, their power increases exponentially, all effects based in Facet start to use Facet +1, including the effects of Dynamic Excellences. Each dot of Inspiration from that point on increase the effects of Facets by 1, up to Facet +5 at Inspiration 10.<br /> Novas have one additional trait, Flux, that measures overuse of their powers, going from 0 to 10.<br /> Whenever the Nova would receive the Telluric Burnout condition, the Nova instead gains 1 point of Flux.<br /> If a Nova spends an entire scene interacting with humans without using any of their powers, the Nova lose 1 Flux.<br /> If the Flux ever reach 10, the Nova lose all Quantum Flux and gains a Transformation, that change the Nova\u2019s appearance, physiology or psychology, making the Nova feel less human To them selves or the others.<br /> <br /> A few comments:<br /> -Need to work in a list of Gifts per Aptitude and Tier<br /> -Need to create the advanced gifts of each aptitude (read 4-5 mode dots)<br /> -Need to create the quantakinesis gifts (there are too few of them)<br /> -House Rules: Inspiration will be an Adventure! CC, so it may take some time\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-28-2022, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T07:02:23-08:00","id":1501698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1491109-more-power-psions-and-novas-under-the-talent-rules?p=1491434#post1491434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am willing to spend some of my free time here to organize the gifts from Adventure by themes and modes. If anyone have done it before it would make it FAR easier to me...</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this isn't too little too late.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<b>Biological Gifts</b><br /> My initial thought was that Biological Gifts should get subdivided between Biokinesis and Vitakinesis. But far too many of them as written tend to have more in common with Clairsentience or Telepathy; so I ended up dividing these more ways:<br /> <br /> <u>Biokinesis</u>:<br /> <i>Adaptation: </i>Darwin's Razor<br /> <i>Psychomorphing: </i>Density, Made of Rubber, Mind Over Matter, Reflex Booster, Stiff as a Board, Supreme Flexibility, Telluric Enhancement, Traversing the Impassable, Treading Death's Path, Walking on the Water<br /> <i>Transmogrify: </i>Face of Clay<br /> <br /> <u>Vitakinesis</u>:<br /> <i>Iatrosis: </i>Ascetic Trance, Command the Many Meridians, Push the Pain Away, Read the Wounds, Touch of Life<br /> <i>Augendis</i>: Human Battery<br /> <i>Algesis</i>: Pain Amplification, Phantom Pain, Slow, Stop<br /> <br /> <u>Clairsentience</u>:<br /> <i>Psychometry: </i>Dead Minds Tell Some Tales<br /> <i>Psycholocation: </i>Find the Weak Link, Over Your Shoulder, Sympathetic Link, Unmoored Perceptions<br /> <i>Psychocognition: </i>Counter-Gambit, Three Moves Ahead<br /> <br /> <u>Telepathy</u>:<br /> <i>Rapport: </i>All Creatures Great and Small, Check!, Keep Your Friends Close<br /> <i>Psychbending: </i>Brain Jamming, Over There!, Refuge in Banality<br /> <br /> <u>Quantakinesis</u>:<br /> <i>Fundamentals:</i>Telluric Resonance<br /> <br /> <b>Cognitive Gifts</b><br /> These should be divided between Clairsentience and Telepathy.<br /> <br /> <u>Clairsentience</u>:<br /> <i>Psychometry: </i>Hunter and Prey, Medium, That Which Was, Truth of Things<br /> <i>Psycholocation: </i>Dowsing, Marked Man<br /> <i>Psychocognition: </i>Haryspicy<br /> <br /> <u>Telepathy</u>:<br /> <i>Rapport: </i>Annotated Bibliography, Brain Skimming, Friend From Foe, Perfect Translation<br /> <i>Mindshare: </i>Direct Voice, Dream Diver, Dream Transmission, Hive Mind, Mental Crucible, Oneiric Network, Palace of the Mind, Sense Minds, Thoughtography, Veil of the Unseen<br /> <i>Psychbending: </i>Cloak of Dread, Cloud the Mind, Conversational Shortcut, Disorient, Doppelg\u00e4nger, Evil Eye, Hypnotic Sleep, Labyrinth, Monotony, Papers Please, Pavlov's Bell, Psychic Double, Psychic Programming, Queen Takes Pawn, Recursion, Somebody's Watching Me, Terror Manifest<br /> <br /> <b>Energetic</b><br /> These get divided between EK, PK, and a handful of others:<br /> <br /> <u>EK</u>:<br /> <i>Photokinesis: </i>Illuminate<br /> <i>Technokinesis: </i>Gremlin Syndrome, Machine Master<br /> <br /> <u>PK</u>:<br /> <i>Thermokinesis: </i>Hot or Cold, Thermal Event<br /> <i>Telekinesis: </i>Adrift in Etheric Currents, Awash in the Etheric, Fist of the Mind, Halt Flight, Intensifying Grip, Javelin of Will, Levitation, Manipulation Without Touch, Mental Burst, Mindhammer, Psychic Accuracy, Psychic Hand, Seize the Puppet Strings, Strength of the Mind, Teledigitation, Telekinetic Summoning<br /> <i>Perikinesis: </i>Force Cage, Psychic Conjuration<br /> <br /> <u>Telepathy</u>:<br /> <i>Mindshare</i>: Monsters From The Id, Such Stuff as Dreams Are Made Of<br /> <i>Psychbending</i>: Astral Projection, Astral Transference, Brainstorm, Enervating Grasp, Pareidola's Price, Stunning Pulse<br /> <br /> <u>Teleport</u>:<br /> <i>Translocation: </i>Vanishing Act<br /> <i>Transmassion: </i>Sleight of Will<br /> <i>Transportal: </i>Doorway<br /> <br /> <u>Quantakinesis</u>:<br /> <i>Fundamentals: </i>Power Transfer<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u>Clairsentience</u>:<br /> <i>Psycholocation: </i>Telepresent Relay, Tremor Sense<br /> <br /> <b>Conclusions</b> <br /> Just about every Mode of every Aptitude has representation here. The exceptions are EK's Electromanipulation and Quantakinesis's Energetics and Transmutation. I would put any new Gifts based on these Modes under the Energetic Keyword: Electromanipulation and Energetics for obvious reasons, Transmutation because it's the least bad choice. Given that the Teleportation Gifts have the Energetic keyword, that's not much of a stretch at all. <br /> <br /> Other areas where Adventure's Gifts are particularly weak are Quantakinesis's Fundamentals and PK's Perikinesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-30-2023, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T07:43:36-08:00","id":1501704,"title":"","content":"THANK YOU!<br /> <br /> I have done the Quantum part (soon I will post) because its just about letting people get scale (and do some small changes in the thematics to make it easier), but my lazyness and work days have preventd me from doing this part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T07:56:21-08:00","id":1501706,"title":"","content":"Note that the above is a rough draft. I'd also point out that some of the non-BioK/VitaK found under Biological might be thought of as the result of two Aptitudes working together, with either BioK or VitaK unlocking, e.g., a Telepathy power that wouldn't otherwise be available. <br /> <br /> I'll revise the post to split each entry among the Modes. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T08:18:52-08:00","id":1501708,"title":"","content":"Sure! There are a few gifts that work for more than one Aptitude (like Astral Projetion work for Telepathy and Clair) with different descriptions of the fluffy.<br /> <br /> In 2 days I will be home and read your list in peace and may start working on the writings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T04:51:10-08:00","id":1503368,"title":"","content":"Quick update on my ideas for Novas as empowered Stalwarts.<br /> <br /> Stalwarts have basically 2 different kinds of Gifts, Attribute Gifts and Power Gifts.<br /> Novas have access to the same gifts, but they can have some of those gifts more than once.<br /> - Most Attribute Gifts can only be taken once, except Scion of Humanity (see bellow)<br /> - Most Power Gifts can only be taken once, except a few (see bellow).<br /> <br /> Scion of Humanity can be taken multiple times, no more than 1 per dot in the related Facet, split the followin way:<br /> - Might: once per dot in Destructive Facet<br /> - Cunning or Dexterity: once per dot in Intuitive Facet<br /> - Composure or Intelect: once per in Reflective Facet<br /> - Presence or Manipulation: once per dot in Intuitive Facet<br /> - Stamina or Resolve: once per dot in Reflective Facet<br /> So if you have Intuitive 2, you can pick Scion of Humanity twice for Dexterity or twice Cunning or once for Dexterity and once for Cunning.<br /> <br /> Power Gifts that has no prerequisites in other gifts can be taken a second time onde the character has raised all facets to 2 or more, and again when all facets are 3 or more and so on.<br /> The number of times the gift is taken defines the scale of the effect of the chosen gift and all the related other power gifts (gifts with prerequisete in the gift or prerequisite in the gifts with prerequeisite in that gift and so on).<br /> So if you have a Gift that let you make your hand hot, and pick it twice, the heat scale of your hand will be 2, so cause damage scale 2. If that gift let you pick a gift that let you shoot fire from your hands, that fire will have power scale 2, and if a third gift (with prerequisite in the second gift) let you fly with the fire jets you throw in the ground, the flight speed will be scale 2.<br /> <br /> That put your nova on the 1-5 scale, but Novas can go beyond.<br /> When a Nova reach Inspiration 6, all facets are treated as 1 higher than original to define how many times the gifts can be taken.<br /> At Inspiration 7 it increase by 1 (to +2), Inspiration 8 by 1 again (+3) and so on until Inspiration 10 that increase all to 10 (5 from the facet +5)<br /> So lets say a Nova has facets D0 I3 R4 (Inspiration 5), if he increase Reflective Facet to 5 the Inspiration is 6. and so, to define the number of time the Nova can take the relates gifts is as if the facets were D1 I4 R6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}